[The Start of Assistant 1’s Answer]
There is no specific age at which the human brain, including the prefrontal cortex, reaches full maturity. Changes in structure and myelination of gray matter continue to occur throughout adult life, with different mental abilities peaking at different times. Some abilities may peak around the time of high school graduation, while others may not peak until much later, even into one's 40s or beyond. The misconception may arise because certain legal milestones (e.g., ages 18, 21, 25) are often associated with reaching "adulthood" or maturity, but this does not necessarily have a direct correlation with brain development.
